  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1033 PM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nA surface boundary will push southward across Middle Tennessee\nlate Tuesday or Tuesday evening. There are low to medium rain and\nstorm chances with this frontal passage, but perhaps the most\nsignificant impact will be a cooler and less humid air mass, so\nthat the heat threat will end after Tuesday as temperatures drop\nback to seasonal normals. Also, rain and storm chances from\nWednesday through the remainder of the week will be very low.\nHowever, this coming weekend will likely be another wet one as the\nnext active weather system spreads into the mid state from the\nArklatex region.",
